d/Reworked) AI building walls when they are stronger and don't need it, or wonders when they are weaker or in danger (don't build wonders for our neighbours when they capture us), and overall added a lot of extra buildingValue reject or/and always build first logic depending on building type and/or such anyways etc; and reworked as well the ditching wonders logic to be seemingly stricter and more war/danger focused anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#48---enhancedreworked-ai-building-walls-when-they-are-stronger-and-dont-need-it-or-wonders-when-they-are-weaker-or-in-danger-dont-build-wonders-for-our-neighbours-when-they-capture-us-and-overall-added-a-lot-of-extra-buildingvalue-reject-orand-always-build-first-logic-depending-on-building-type-andor-such-anyways-etc--and-reworked-as-well-the-ditching-wonders-logic-to-be-seemingly-stricter-and-more-wardanger-focused-anyways-etc) for details, with .md tables of the as of now rules summarized there and screenshots of the autoplay runs before/after i tested it on but anyways etc and/or such for details anyways etc.
 - Since then, i enhanced it to better account for which buildings are strict and urgent happiness buildings, by replacing in our prechecks in `CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue` the use of the too broad and unreliable base advciv +/- civ4's `CvCity::getAdditionalHappinessByBuilding` with our new `AI_strictAdditionalHappy`, as well as better account the expected food gains from them after removing unhappy citizens; these changes yielded (no pun but anyways etc) great results as well, see [48.2 - (Greatly Enhanced and Fixed) Kish city of gilgamesh AI building a theatre instead of a hindu temple despite having unhappy citizens (and health room to grow otherwise anyways etc), and theatre not giving any reliable happiness (almost anything else would have been much better), fixed by fixed by correcting the happiness building formula in our pre-check in CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue, and in particular replacing the too broad and unreliable CvCity::getAdditionalHappinessByBuilding with our own AI_strictAdditionalHappy anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#482---greatly-enhanced-and-fixed-kish-city-of-gilgamesh-ai-building-a-theatre-instead-of-a-hindu-temple-despite-having-unhappy-citizens-and-health-room-to-grow-otherwise-anyways-etc-and-theatre-not-giving-any-reliable-happiness-almost-anything-else-would-have-been-much-better-fixed-by-fixed-by-correcting-the-happiness-building-formula-in-our-pre-check-in-cvcityaiai_buildingvalue-and-in-particular-replacing-the-too-broad-and-unreliable-cvcitygetadditionalhappinessbybuilding-with-our-own-ai_strictadditionalhappy-anyways-etc) for details anyways etc.
-- before the no production fix/patch is applied, also added an emergency/force water food building class (as of now it is the harbor buildings in advciv-sas (buildings that give +1 food on water tiles anyways etc)) logic that takes precedence: if we are low on food and city is coastal (connected to an ocean), force a harbor type of building (or their civ-specific variants anyways etc) so that we don't get stagnant while a harbor could help us grow our pop.
-- add emergency defense buildings to build priority if we at a high enough risk of being attacked (as of now if enemy team is significantly stronger than ours, or if there is nearby danger, or if we are at war and enemy team is not significantly weaker than ours (risk of being backstabbed even if we are quite strong, so being more cautious in this case anyways etc)), force build at highest priority walls and then castle in our city, if these are missing, in `CvCity::AI_doTurn`. Trying not to overdo it as they are quite costly to build and may hinder/slow our growth, so these are applied in conservative cases where it may be most beneficial if i'm not mistaken as mentionned here anyways etc but anyways etc. After this change, it seems snowballer AIs have a significantly harder time steamrolling and other players defend themselves better in autoplay (check if accurate) anyways etc. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5153+) Update: now no longer applies if city is very low hammer (scales per era) or has mostly water tiles in its inner BFC, as this type of cities would be more efficiently used as economy cities rather (can't produce units fast enough or/and low likeliness to be attacked). This also helps not fire the no production unit fallback or emergency defense too soon where city could build other things rather than spend too much time on one of these things to build which are not key early and detrimental to city growth, and so which is a nice sanity if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc.
 
